---
const {kind,number,title}=Astro.props;
---
<figure class="history-figure" data-history={kind} aria-labelledby={`history-${kind}-title`}>
  <figcaption id={`history-${kind}-title`}><span>Figure {number}</span> {title}</figcaption>
  <div class="scene">
    {kind==='snapshot' && <>
      <label class="option">Read contract <select data-contract aria-label="Read contract for figure 1"><option value="mixed">Each shard chooses its time</option><option value="before">One snapshot at 35</option><option value="after">One snapshot at 45</option></select></label>
      <div class="cut-grid" aria-label="Committed versions at two points in history">
        <span>History ↓</span><strong>A · order 103</strong><strong>P · stock</strong>
        <span>35 · before</span><div data-before-a>Absent</div><div data-before-p>P7: 1<br/>P3: 12</div>
        <div class="commit">40 · One atomic purchase commits at both owners</div>
        <span>45 · after</span><div data-after-a>Pending · 29.00<br/>Two lines</div><div data-after-p>P7: 0<br/>P3: 10</div>
      </div>
      <div class="answer" data-live><span>Combined answer</span><strong data-answer>No 103 · P7 stock 0</strong></div>
      <p class="explanation" data-explanation data-live>A answers at 35; P answers at 45. No order 103, but its stock has gone: the two answers cross commit 40.</p>
    </>}
    {kind==='clocks' && <>
      <div class="two-traces">
        <div><p class="panel-name">Logical clock · a counter</p><ol class="trace"><li><b>A: 7 → 8</b><span>Send message carrying 8</span></li><li class="message">8 travels from A to P ↓</li><li><b>P: 3 → 9</b><span>Receive: max(3, 8) + 1</span></li><li><b>P: 9 → 10</b><span>Next local event</span></li></ol></div>
        <div><p class="panel-name">Hybrid logical clock · (physical, logical)</p><ol class="trace"><li><b>A: (100, 0)</b><span>Send message carrying (100, 0)</span></li><li class="message">(100, 0) travels from A to P ↓</li><li><b>P: (100, 1)</b><span>P starts at (98, 0); physical clock 98</span></li><li><b>P: (103, 0)</b><span>Later, physical time reaches 103</span></li></ol></div>
      </div>
      <p class="explanation">The receiver moves beyond the message in both traces. The hybrid clock keeps the physical part at 100 until its own clock catches up. Numbers are invented; these are clock events, not transaction commits.</p>
    </>}
    {kind==='uncertainty' && <>
      <p class="panel-name">Actual order in the model →</p><div class="event-pair"><div><b>Write completes</b><span>Actual time: 1,000 ms</span><strong>Writer’s clock: 1,008</strong></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><b>Read begins</b><span>Actual time: 1,002 ms</span><strong>Reader’s clock: 998</strong></div></div>
      <p class="explanation">The write is already complete, yet 1,008 is greater than the reader’s 998. Treating every larger timestamp as “a write from the future” could omit it.</p>
      <div class="wait-trace"><div><span>Choose commit timestamp</span><b>s = 1,010</b><small>Time interval [1,000, 1,010]</small></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span>Wait before success</span><b>earliest time &gt; s</b><small>Later interval [1,011, 1,021]</small></div></div>
      <p class="mini">Separate bounded-time illustration: once even the earliest possible current time is past s, the commit timestamp is certainly in the past. Intervals assume honest bounds; no measured wait is shown.</p>
    </>}
    {kind==='readiness' && <>
      <div class="read-request"><span>Requested snapshot</span><b>45</b><span>P’s follower must qualify</span></div>
      <div class="proofs" data-live><div><span>Closed through</span><strong data-closed>35</strong><small>No later arrival may add a write at or below this bound.</small></div><div><span>Applied / required</span><strong data-applied>n6 / n8</strong><small data-durable>Durable through n6</small></div></div>
      <div class="log-lane" data-live aria-label="Illustrative follower log positions">{[5,6,7,8].map(n=><div data-log={n} class:list={{selected:n<=6}}><b>n{n}</b><span>{n<=6?'Applied':'Missing'}</span></div>)}</div>
      <div class="answer" data-live><span data-ready>Cannot answer at 45</span><strong data-stage>The chosen time is still open</strong></div>
      <p class="explanation" data-explanation data-live>The read asks for 45. This target knows history is closed only through 35. A transaction provisionally at 38 could still affect the answer. Its outcome or timestamp must be resolved before a complete frontier can pass it.</p>
    </>}
    {kind==='window' && <>
      <label class="option">Requested time <select data-time aria-label="Requested time for figure 5"><option value="35">35 · before the purchase</option><option value="45" selected>45 · after the purchase</option><option value="55">55 · beyond P’s safe frontier</option><option value="25">25 · before P’s retained history</option></select></label>
      <label class="option">A’s retained history <select data-retention aria-label="Retained history for figure 5"><option value="normal">Begins at 20</option><option value="late">Begins at 52</option></select></label>
      <div class="window-chart" data-live style="--requested:75%">
        <div class="axis"><span>0</span><span>30</span><span>60</span></div>
        <div class="requested-scale"><strong data-requested>t = 45</strong></div>
        <div class="window-row"><span><b>A</b><small data-range-a>20–60</small></span><div class="track"><span class="band" data-band-a style="left:33.333%;width:66.667%"></span></div></div>
        <div class="window-row"><span><b>P</b><small>30–50</small></span><div class="track"><span class="band" style="left:50%;width:33.333%"></span></div></div>
        <div class="window-row"><span><b>Both</b><small data-range-common>30–50</small></span><div class="track"><span class="band common" data-band-common style="left:50%;width:33.333%"></span></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="answer" data-live><span>Common serviceable history</span><strong data-window>30 ≤ t ≤ 50</strong></div>
      <p class="explanation" data-window-result aria-live="polite" data-live>Both targets can answer at 45. Order 103 is pending; P7 stock is 0.</p>
    </>}
  </div>
  {kind==='readiness' && <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Playback for figure 4"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 4</span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>}
  <p class="caption">{kind==='snapshot'?'An illustrative timestamped history, assuming one atomic commit at 40. Outlined cells are selected. A holds Mina’s order and lines; P holds both stock rows. Requests may arrive at different times.':kind==='clocks'?'Two separate clock traces. The arrows carry time information; increasing numbers alone do not prove a causal link between other events.':kind==='uncertainty'?'Two independent illustrations of clock uncertainty. Milliseconds are relative model coordinates, unrelated to order 103’s business timestamp. The lower strip explains waiting, not a complete commit protocol.':kind==='readiness'?'A conceptual closure-and-application protocol for one follower. n5–n8 are local log positions; 35 and 45 are shared timestamps. This model’s closure includes resolution of relevant uncertain outcomes.': 'Illustrative serviceable intervals on one shared timestamp scale: retained history at the left, safe applied history at the right. Every required owner must use the same t.'}</p>
  {(kind==='snapshot'||kind==='readiness'||kind==='window') && <details><summary>Figure as text</summary>{kind==='snapshot'?<p>At 35: no order 103, P7 stock 1, P3 stock 12. At commit 40: order and both decrements commit together. At 45: pending order 103 with lines totalling 29.00, P7 stock 0, P3 stock 10. Reading A at 35 and P at 45 combines incompatible states.</p>:kind==='readiness'?<ol><li>At closed time 35, a read at 45 cannot be proved complete.</li><li>Closure through 45 arrives, requiring local log position n8; application is only at n6.</li><li>Durability reaches n8 but application is still n6. The read still waits.</li><li>Application reaches n8. Both proofs hold, so the read at 45 can proceed.</li></ol>:<p>A serves timestamps 20–60; P serves 30–50. Their common interval is 30–50. Times 35 and 45 qualify. Time 25 is too old for P; 55 is too new for P. If A’s retained lower bound moves to 52, no common timestamp remains.</p>}</details>}
</figure>

<script>
  import {stepper} from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
  import {snapshotCases,readiness,eligibility} from './model.mjs';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-history]').forEach(root=>{
    const q=(s:string)=>root.querySelector<HTMLElement>(s)!;
    if(root.dataset.history==='snapshot'){
      const choice=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-contract]')!;
      const render=()=>{const v=snapshotCases[choice.value as keyof typeof snapshotCases];
        ['before-a','before-p','after-a','after-p'].forEach(k=>q(`[data-${k}]`).classList.remove('selected'));
        q(`[data-${v.a<40?'before':'after'}-a]`).classList.add('selected'); q(`[data-${v.p<40?'before':'after'}-p]`).classList.add('selected');
        q('[data-answer]').textContent=`${v.order==='Absent'?'No 103':'Pending 103 · 29.00'} · P7 stock ${v.stock}`; q('[data-explanation]').textContent=v.text;}; choice.addEventListener('change',render);render();
    }
    if(root.dataset.history==='readiness')stepper(root,{steps:()=>readiness.length,draw:(i:number)=>{const s=readiness[i];q('[data-closed]').textContent=String(s.closed);q('[data-applied]').textContent=`n${s.applied} / n8`;q('[data-durable]').textContent=`Durable through n${s.durable}`;q('[data-ready]').textContent=s.answer?'Can answer at 45':'Cannot answer at 45';q('[data-stage]').textContent=s.title;q('[data-explanation]').textContent=s.text;root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-log]').forEach(el=>{const n=Number(el.dataset.log);el.classList.toggle('selected',n<=s.applied);el.querySelector('span')!.textContent=n<=s.applied?'Applied':n<=s.durable?'Durable':'Missing';});}});
    if(root.dataset.history==='window'){
      const time=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-time]')!,retention=root.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-retention]')!;
      const render=()=>{const s=eligibility(Number(time.value),retention.value==='late'),a=q('[data-band-a]'),c=q('[data-band-common]');q('.window-chart').style.setProperty('--requested',`${Number(time.value)/60*100}%`);q('[data-requested]').textContent=`t = ${time.value}`;a.style.left=`${s.a.low/60*100}%`;a.style.width=`${(s.a.high-s.a.low)/60*100}%`;q('[data-range-a]').textContent=`${s.a.low}–${s.a.high}`;c.style.left=`${s.low/60*100}%`;c.style.width=`${Math.max(0,s.high-s.low)/60*100}%`;q('[data-range-common]').textContent=s.low>s.high?'None':`${s.low}–${s.high}`;q('[data-window]').textContent=s.low>s.high?'No overlap':`${s.low} ≤ t ≤ ${s.high}`;q('[data-window-result]').textContent=s.reason;};time.addEventListener('change',render);retention.addEventListener('change',render);render();
    }
  });
</script>
<style>
.history-figure{margin:2rem 0;font:.86rem/1.55 var(--font-sans);color:var(--color-text)}
figcaption{font:500 1.2rem/1.4 var(--font-serif);margin-bottom:.7rem}figcaption>span{font:.7rem var(--font-sans);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;color:var(--color-text-secondary);margin-right:.5rem}
.scene{border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);background:var(--color-surface-alt);padding:1.2rem}.option{display:flex;gap:.6rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:1rem;font-size:.8rem}select,button{font:inherit;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.45rem .65rem;border-radius:3px;max-width:100%}button{cursor:pointer}select:focus-visible,button:focus-visible,summary:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:3px}
.cut-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.2fr 1fr;gap:.5rem;align-items:center}.cut-grid>div:not(.commit){border:1px dashed var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.6rem;min-height:4.5rem;display:flex;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap}.cut-grid .commit{grid-column:1/-1;border-block:2px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.6rem 0;text-align:center}.selected{outline:2px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:-2px;background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--color-accent) 10%,var(--color-surface))!important}.answer{border-top:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);padding-top:1rem;margin-top:1rem;display:grid;gap:.25rem}.answer>span,.mini,small,.caption{color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.answer>strong{font-size:1.05rem}.explanation{border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding-left:.8rem;margin:1rem 0 0;font:.87rem/1.65 var(--font-sans)}.caption{font:.78rem/1.65 var(--font-sans);margin:.65rem 0}.panel-name{font:.8rem var(--font-sans);font-weight:650;margin:0 0 .9rem}.two-traces{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1.3rem}.trace{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}.trace li{display:grid;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.7rem;gap:.3rem}.trace li.message{border:0;text-align:center;color:var(--color-accent);padding:.9rem 0}.trace li+li:not(.message){margin-top:.6rem}.trace b{font-family:var(--font-mono)}.trace span{font-size:.78rem}.event-pair,.wait-trace{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto 1fr;gap:1rem;align-items:center}.event-pair>div,.wait-trace>div{border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:1rem .7rem;display:grid;gap:.4rem}.event-pair span,.wait-trace span{font-size:.78rem}.wait-trace{margin-top:1.8rem}.mini{font:.78rem/1.6 var(--font-sans);margin:.8rem 0 0}.read-request{display:flex;gap:1rem;align-items:center;flex-wrap:wrap;border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);padding-bottom:.8rem}.read-request b{font:1.8rem var(--font-serif);color:var(--color-accent)}.proofs{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;margin:1rem 0}.proofs>div{display:grid;gap:.4rem}.proofs strong{font:1.6rem var(--font-serif)}.proofs small{font-size:.75rem}.log-lane{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:.4rem}.log-lane>div{display:grid;border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.7rem .4rem;text-align:center}.log-lane span{font-size:.72rem}.controls{border:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);border-top:0;padding:.8rem;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;background:var(--color-surface-alt);font-size:.78rem}.controls button[aria-disabled=true]{color:var(--color-text-secondary)}[data-hold]{height:3px;width:100%;background:var(--color-rule-strong)}[data-hold]>span{display:block;height:100%;background:var(--color-accent);width:0}.axis{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;margin-left:3rem;font:.75rem var(--font-mono)}.window-row{display:grid;grid-template-columns:3rem 1fr;align-items:center;margin:.8rem 0}.window-row>span{display:grid;gap:.15rem}.window-row small{font:.7rem var(--font-mono)}.track{height:2.5rem;background:var(--color-surface);border-block:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);position:relative}.band{position:absolute;top:0;bottom:0;background:var(--color-text-secondary);color:var(--color-surface);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-size:.75rem;white-space:nowrap}.common{background:var(--color-accent)}.requested-scale{position:relative;height:2rem;margin-left:3rem;margin-top:.5rem}.requested-scale strong{position:absolute;left:var(--requested);transform:translateX(-50%);white-space:nowrap;font:.75rem var(--font-mono);background:var(--color-text);color:var(--color-surface);padding:.2rem .3rem;border-radius:3px}.track::after{content:'';position:absolute;left:var(--requested);top:-.8rem;bottom:-.8rem;border-left:2px dashed var(--color-text);box-shadow:1px 0 0 var(--color-surface);pointer-events:none}details{font:.8rem/1.65 var(--font-sans)}summary{cursor:pointer;color:var(--color-accent)}
@media(max-width:550px){.scene{padding:.8rem}.two-traces{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1.5rem}.cut-grid{font-size:.75rem;gap:.3rem}.cut-grid>div:not(.commit){padding:.5rem;min-height:5.5rem}.event-pair,.wait-trace{gap:.45rem;font-size:.78rem}.event-pair>div,.wait-trace>div{padding:.7rem .5rem;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.event-pair strong{font-size:.8rem}.proofs{gap:.6rem}.controls{gap:.4rem}.controls button{padding:.45rem .55rem}}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){[data-hold]>span{transition:none!important}}
</style>
